  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Genus of flowering plants}}\n{{Automatic taxobox\n|image = Starr_010520-0107_Ciclospermum_leptophyllum.jpg\n|image_caption = ''Cyclospermum leptophyllum''\n|display_parents = 2\n|taxon = Cyclospermum\n|authority = [[Lag.]]\n|subdivision_ranks = Species\n|subdivision = 3, see text\n}}\n\n'''''Cyclospermum''''' (also, '''''Ciclospermum''''') is a small genus of plants in the family [[Apiaceae]]. There are three species, including the well-known weed ''[[Cyclospermum leptophyllum]]'', the marsh parsley or fir-leafed celery.\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n==External links==\n* [http://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/cgi-bin/get_JM_treatment.pl?329,361 Jepson Manual Treatment]\n* [https://plants.usda.gov/java/profile?symbol=CYCLO4 USDA Plants Profile]\n\n{{Taxonbar|from1=Q2709792|from2=Q87293233}}\n\n[[Category:Apioideae]]\n{{Apiaceae-stub}}",
